From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:11:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: bind local-out flows to PON again

The vendor 6.18 feed stopped the PON transmit path from calling the
transmit bind handler, because that call bound forwarded flows before
their flow table entry existed. The handler is also the only place
that binds a local-out flow. Each local-out packet to PON therefore
went back to the CPU through the metered ring, and an upload from the
router over PON stayed at the rate of that meter.

The PON transmit path calls the handler again for local-out packets.
Forwarded flows keep the vendor behavior.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_ppe.c |    8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/arht_ppe.c
@@ -2992,9 +2992,11 @@ void airoha_ppe_foe_flow_update_pon_offl
 unlock:
 	spin_unlock_bh(&ppe_lock);
 
-	/* This block is intentionally kept for symmetry but will not be
-     * triggered since flow_table_enable is always 1 in this function. */
-	if(flow_table_enable == 0)
+	/* The note at the top does not hold for a local-out flow: it has no
+	 * flow table entry, and only this handler binds it. The handler
+	 * binds only an unbound entry, so a bound flow is safe.
+	 */
+	if(flow_table_enable == 0 || airoha_is_local_out(skb))
 	{
 		airoha_ppe_tx_handler(skb, pinfo, 2);
 	}
